# Projects carousel hover and click

The spotlight slides after the pointer has hovered the **left or right side** for **1 continuous second**, or **immediately** when that side is clicked.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — overlap the next hover wait with the in-progress slide (~100ms gap)
wait = Math.max(DWELL_MS, lockedUntil - now);

// ✅ GOOD — first hover waits 1s; later holds wait until the slide finishes, then a longer pause
const DWELL_MS = 1000;
const FOLLOWUP_DWELL_MS = 1600;
wait = remainingLock + (chained ? FOLLOWUP_DWELL_MS : DWELL_MS);
onMouseEnter={() => startDwell(sideNeighbor)};
onMouseLeave={() => cancelDwell()};
onClick={() => advanceSide("left" | "right")};
```

Do not skip the hover dwell with a shorter timeout or auto-advance. Click may skip the dwell, but still wait out an in-progress slide. After a slide, if the pointer is still on that side, wait for the motion to finish **plus** the follow-up dwell before sliding again. Keep the motion a smooth 3D slide between the five Figma layouts (~0.9s). Translucent left/right chevrons appear while that side is hovered.
